          "detail": {
            "simple": "The update happened without you noticing anything.",
            "tech": "Zero-duplicate deployment."
          }
        }
      ],
      "explain": [
        {
          "simple": "During an update, Kubernetes no longer stops the worker at once. It asks it to stop and gives it time to finish the task it has started.",
          "tech": "Graceful shutdown: catch SIGTERM, accept no new jobs, finish and ack the running job; set terminationGracePeriodSeconds accordingly."
        },
        {
          "simple": "So the worker still reports “done” before it stops. The waiting list ticks the question off and does not hand it out again.",
          "tech": "With the ack before exit there is no redelivery. As an extra safety net, an idempotency check by job ID is recommended."
        }
      ]
